-- First-person detect: duels force FP, lobby is TP. Camera-mode CFrame
-- writes lose to the game's FP camera (it hard-sets every frame AFTER our
-- step), so FP always aims via mousemoverel ??" the game consumes mouse look.
-- Finite guard: WorldToViewportPoint and prediction math can hand back
-- inf/nan (degenerate/respawning parts). Feeding those into mousemoverel
-- or CFrame.lookAt spikes the frame and hard-crashes some executors ??"
-- this is the "press key, lag, crash" chain. Anything non-finite drops
-- the lock instead of moving.
function hubFiniteNum(x)
    return type(x) == "number" and x == x and math.abs(x) ~= math.huge
end


function hubFiniteVec(v)
    local ok = false
    pcall(function()
        ok = hubFiniteNum(v.X) and hubFiniteNum(v.Y) and hubFiniteNum(v.Z)
    end)
