--[[
  ESP FIX FROM V2:
  -----------------
  The v2 ESP drew boxes based on WorldToViewportPoint of character parts,
  but never accounted for DEAD characters whose model persists a few frames
  after death (Humanoid Health = 0 but Character still exists). The esp was
  drawing "ghost boxes" on dead bodies because it only checked modelAlive()
  once before drawing but the character.Parent stayed non-nil.


  Fix: check modelAlive() at the top of every per-player ESP update, and
  explicitly hide + skip the moment Health drops to 0. Also added a
  CharacterRemoving connection to hard-hide all drawings immediately.


  The "stays where body is" bug: this happened because we were caching
  the last computed 2D box position and never clearing it. Now we always
  recompute from live WorldToViewportPoint every frame and call hideESP()
  the moment modelAlive() fails.
]]


